## Feature user guides (`docs/features/`)

**User-facing docs** — what the app does and how to use it. Not progress trackers (those stay in RFC/backlog/issue).

Index: [features/README.md](../../docs/features/README.md) · Template: [TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/features/TEMPLATE.md)

### When to update (mandatory — same turn as code)

Update the matching feature doc **whenever user-visible behavior changes** — not only when an RFC ships.

| Code change | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Nav tab added/removed/renamed, shell chrome, default tabs | [getting-started/navigation.md](../../docs/features/getting-started/navigation.md) · [settings/navigation-bar.md](../../docs/features/settings/navigation-bar.md) |
| Settings screen: new toggle, moved section, renamed label | Matching `docs/features/settings/*.md` |
| Player controls, PiP, subtitles, speed, next episode | Matching `docs/features/playback/*.md` |
| Scraper/source/provider behavior users configure or see | `docs/features/scrapers/*` · `docs/features/sources/*` |
| Tab feature UX (`apps/forja/lib/features/<name>/`) | Matching `docs/features/**/<name>.md` (or add one) |
| Platform limits (torrent hidden, constrained profile) | Affected feature doc + [platforms.md](../../docs/features/getting-started/platforms.md) if cross-cutting |
| Feature ships (was stub / coming soon) | Move doc out of `coming-soon/`; add to [features README](../../docs/features/README.md) |
| Feature removed or permanently disabled | Update doc honestly or move to coming-soon with “removed” note — do not describe dead UI |

### What to keep accurate

Each feature file ([TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/features/TEMPLATE.md)) must reflect **current** app behavior:

- **How to open it** — nav path, settings path, entry points (must match live UI)
- **What you can do** — actions the user can actually perform today
- **Setup** — keys, OAuth, URLs the settings screen still uses
- **Tips / Related** — cross-links still valid

**Read the code or run the UI before editing.** Do not copy from RFCs or stale docs — code is source of truth ([honesty-and-completion.mdc](./honesty-and-completion.mdc)).

### New or renamed features

1. Create or rename `docs/features/<category>/<slug>.md` from [TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/features/TEMPLATE.md)
2. Add link in [features/README.md](../../docs/features/README.md) (and **I want to…** table if user-facing)
3. Grep `docs/features/` for old slug/path and fix cross-links

RFC/issue/backlog track **ship status**; feature docs track **how it works for users**. Both update in the same turn when behavior changes.

